# Git on Windows has core.autocrlf=true here, which means it rewrites line
# endings in anything it decides is text. It decided the generated PDF was
# text, and warned that it would turn every LF into CRLF on the next checkout -
# which silently corrupts a PDF for anyone who clones the repository. The file
# committed fine; it is the checkout that would break it.
#
# So the formats that must never be touched are named explicitly.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.crx   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
